      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the possible degrees of the remainder when a polynomial \\( P(x) \\) of degree \\( n \\) is divided by \\( 2x^2 - 7x + 18 \\), we can use the polynomial division algorithm. This algorithm states that for any polynomial \\( P(x) \\) of degree \\( n \\) and any non-zero polynomial \\( D(x) \\) of degree \\( m \\), we can express \\( P(x) \\) as:\n\n\\[ P(x) = (2x^2 - 7x + 18)Q(x) + R(x), \\]\n\nwhere \\( Q(x) \\) is the quotient and \\( R(x) \\) is the remainder. The degree of the remainder \\( R(x) \\) must be less than the degree of \\( D(x) \\). Here, the degree of \\( 2x^2 - 7x + 18 \\) is 2. Therefore, the possible degrees of the remainder \\( R(x) \\) are 0 or 1. If the degree of \\( R(x) \\) were 2 or greater, it would contradict the form of the quotient and remainder.\n\nThus, the possible degrees of the remainder are:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0, 1}\n\\]",
