      "text": "To determine the possible degrees of the remainder when a polynomial \\( P(x) \\) is divided by \\( 2x^2 - 7x + 18 \\), we need to use the polynomial division algorithm. The polynomial division algorithm states that for any polynomials \\( P(x) \\) and \\( D(x) \\) (where \\( D(x) \\neq 0 \\)), there exist unique polynomials \\( Q(x) \\) (the quotient) and \\( R(x) \\) (the remainder) such that:\n\n\\[ P(x) = D(x) \\cdot Q(x) + R(x) \\]\n\nwhere the degree of \\( R(x) \\) is less than the degree of \\( D(x) \\).\n\nIn this problem, \\( D(x) = 2x^2 - 7x + 18 \\), which is a polynomial of degree 2. Therefore, the possible degrees of the remainder \\( R(x) \\) must be less than 2. This means the possible degrees of \\( R(x) \\) are 0 or 1.\n\nLet's summarize the possible degrees of the remainder:\n1. The degree of the remainder can be 0 (a constant term).\n2. The degree of the remainder can be 1 (a linear polynomial).\n\nThus, the possible degrees of the remainder are \\(\\boxed{0, 1}\\).",
